# Defaults for running the CI workflows locally with nektos/act.
#
#   make ci-act              # the whole CI workflow — start here
#   act -j architecture      # one job
#
# The workflows live in ci/workflows, not .github/workflows: CI runs here,
# with act, and never on GitHub. -W points every act invocation at the one
# committed CI workflow, so `act -j lint` runs the same file `make ci-act`
# does, and release.yml (which needs a tag) is left out.
#
# On OrbStack, export DOCKER_HOST first — act does not read the docker context,
# so it looks for /var/run/docker.sock and reports "Couldn't get a valid docker
# connection" even though the docker CLI works:
#
#   export DOCKER_HOST="unix://$HOME/.orbstack/run/docker.sock"
#
# Two things act cannot do, so a green local run is necessary but not sufficient:
#
#   - It only runs Linux containers, so the macos-latest and windows-latest legs
#     of the test matrix cannot run — and those are the reason the matrix exists,
#     since the scaffolder branches on runtime.GOOS in interpreter discovery,
#     venv paths, start scripts and the --install target.
#   - The runner image is not GitHub's. catthehacker/ubuntu is close, but a
#     failure that depends on preinstalled tooling can differ.
#
# The image is pinned to the medium variant: act-latest is ~1GB and carries a
# full toolchain we do not need, since setup-go installs Go itself.
-W ci/workflows/ci.yml

-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-22.04

# Match the host so Apple Silicon runs natively instead of emulating amd64,
# which is several times slower.
--container-architecture linux/arm64

# Run one job at a time.
#
# act shares a single host directory across every job it runs, where real GitHub
# Actions gives each job its own checkout on its own runner. Run concurrently,
# the architecture job regenerates golden files while the test job is reading
# them, and the test job fails for a reason that cannot happen on GitHub.
--concurrent-jobs 1

# Pin the test matrix to the one leg act can actually run.
#
# Without this, `act push` fails on the test job with "Error: invalid reference
# format" before a single test runs: the legs above have no -P mapping, so act
# resolves an empty image name and Docker rejects it. The legs are not skipped,
# which is what this file used to claim — the whole job fails, so the only job
# that runs the suite under -race has never once run locally.
--matrix os:ubuntu-latest
